       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is commercial contract advisory important for businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Commercial contracts define relationships, obligations, risks, and expectations. Effective contract advisory helps businesses protect value, avoid disputes, and create stronger commercial relationships."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Does SHAAS only draft contracts?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. SHAAS provides end-to-end commercial contract advisory, including drafting, review, negotiation support, risk assessment, and contract management frameworks."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS review contracts prepared by another party?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. We regularly assist businesses by reviewing agreements received from customers, suppliers, partners, investors, and other stakeholders."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Does SHAAS support SMEs and startups?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. We support businesses at different stages of growth, from startups establishing their contractual foundations to established organisations managing complex commercial relationships."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS provide ongoing contract support?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. Through flexible advisory arrangements, SHAAS can provide ongoing commercial contract support without requiring businesses to maintain a full-time internal legal team."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Build Stronger Commercial Relationships With SHAAS",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Every successful business relationship depends on clarity, trust, and well-structured agreements."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Whether you are entering a new partnership, negotiating a major transaction, reviewing existing contracts, or building stronger internal contract processes, SHAAS provides the commercial contract advisory support needed to protect your business and support sustainable growth."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Contact SHAAS today to discuss how our Commercial Contract Advisory services can help your organisation reduce risk, strengthen agreements, and create greater commercial confidence."
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
