  {
   "title": "EXTERNAL GENERAL COUNSEL",
   "subtitle": "Senior Legal Leadership Without the Cost of Building an In-House Legal Department",
   "sections": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "As businesses grow, legal matters become increasingly complex."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Contracts become more significant. Regulatory obligations increase. Business decisions involve greater risk. Stakeholders require stronger governance. Management teams need timely legal guidance to make confident decisions."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "However, many organisations are not ready—or do not need—to invest in a full-time General Counsel or build a complete internal legal department."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "At SHAAS, our External General Counsel services in the UAE provide businesses with flexible access to experienced legal advisory support, allowing leadership teams to benefit from senior legal expertise whenever they need it."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "We act as an extension of your management team, providing practical, business-focused legal guidance across contracts, governance, compliance, corporate matters, risk management, and strategic initiatives."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Our approach combines legal expertise with commercial understanding, helping organisations make better decisions, reduce risk, and move forward with confidence."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "A Strategic Legal Partner for Growing Businesses",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "A General Counsel is not simply a lawyer who reviews documents."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "A strong General Counsel understands the business."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "They understand:"
      },
      {
       "type": "list",
       "items": [
        "The company's strategy",
        "Commercial priorities",
        "Operational challenges",
        "Stakeholder expectations",
        "Growth objectives",
        "Risk appetite"
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Traditional legal support is often reactive—businesses contact lawyers when a problem appears."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "An External General Counsel takes a proactive approach by helping organisations identify risks early, establish stronger processes, and integrate legal thinking into everyday business decisions."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS provides this capability through a flexible advisory model designed around your organisation's needs."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Business Challenges We Help Solve",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Businesses typically consider an External General Counsel when they experience challenges such as:"
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "\"We need senior legal support, but hiring a full-time General Counsel is not practical.\""
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Building an internal legal department requires significant investment in:"
      },
      {
       "type": "list",
       "items": [
        "Salaries",
        "Benefits",
        "Recruitment",
        "Training",
        "Management time"
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS provides access to senior legal advisory capability without the fixed cost of a permanent hire."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "\"Our legal matters are becoming too complex for occasional legal support.\""
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "As businesses grow, legal requirements become interconnected."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "A single business decision may involve:"
      },
      {
       "type": "list",
