    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is corporate governance?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Corporate governance refers to the systems, processes, structures, and principles through which organisations are directed, managed, and controlled."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is corporate governance important for businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Effective governance improves decision-making, strengthens accountability, reduces risks, and increases confidence among shareholders, investors, regulators, and other stakeholders."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is corporate governance only relevant for large companies?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Corporate governance is valuable for businesses of all sizes. SMEs and family businesses often benefit significantly from establishing clear structures as they grow."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Does SHAAS help implement governance frameworks?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. SHAAS supports organisations from assessment through implementation, including governance documentation, policies, structures, and ongoing advisory."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "How does corporate governance help family businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Strong governance helps family businesses manage ownership relationships, succession planning, decision-making, and long-term continuity."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Strengthen Your Organisation Through Better Governance",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Strong governance is the foundation of resilient and successful organisations."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Whether you are preparing your business for growth, improving board effectiveness, strengthening investor confidence, or creating a sustainable structure for future generations, SHAAS provides the corporate governance advisory expertise needed to build stronger organisations."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Contact SHAAS today to discuss how our Corporate Governance Advisory services can help your organisation improve decision-making, manage risk, and create long-term value."
      }
     ]
