    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is regulatory compliance advisory?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Regulatory compliance advisory helps organisations understand applicable regulations, assess compliance risks, develop frameworks, and implement processes to meet legal and regulatory obligations."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is regulatory compliance important for businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Effective compliance reduces risk, protects reputation, improves governance, and provides confidence to investors, customers, partners, and regulators."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is compliance only important for regulated industries?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Every business has regulatory obligations relating to areas such as corporate governance, employment, contracts, data protection, taxation, and operational requirements."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS help businesses develop compliance policies?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. SHAAS assists organisations in developing practical policies, procedures, and governance frameworks aligned with their business requirements."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Does SHAAS provide ongoing compliance support?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. Through flexible advisory engagements, SHAAS supports businesses with ongoing compliance reviews, updates, and improvement initiatives."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Build a Stronger Compliance Foundation With SHAAS",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Regulatory complexity is a reality for every growing organisation."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "The businesses that succeed are those that understand their obligations, manage risks proactively, and build compliance into their operations."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS helps organisations transform compliance from a regulatory obligation into a strategic capability that supports trust, resilience, and sustainable growth."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Whether you need a compliance assessment, policy development, regulatory readiness support, or ongoing advisory, our team provides the practical guidance required to operate with confidence."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Contact SHAAS today to discuss how our Regulatory Compliance Advisory services can help your organisation strengthen controls, reduce risks, and prepare for future growth."
