    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is the difference between a Fractional CFO and an accountant?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "An accountant focuses mainly on recording transactions, preparing financial statements, and ensuring compliance. A Fractional CFO focuses on strategy, financial performance, decision-making, and business growth."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Who needs a Fractional CFO?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Fractional CFO services are suitable for SMEs, startups, scale-ups, family businesses, and growing companies that need senior financial expertise without hiring a full-time CFO."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "How often does a Fractional CFO work with a company?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "The engagement frequency depends on the company's needs and may range from periodic strategic reviews to ongoing monthly CFO support."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can a Fractional CFO help improve profitability?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. A Fractional CFO analyses financial performance, cost structures, margins, and business drivers to identify opportunities for improvement."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is a Fractional CFO only useful for companies facing problems?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Many successful companies use Fractional CFO support proactively to strengthen decision-making, prepare for growth, and improve financial discipline."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Strengthen Your Financial Leadership Without Hiring a Full-Time CFO",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Growing businesses need more than accurate financial records. They need financial clarity, strategic insight, and experienced leadership."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
