    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is risk management important for businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Risk management helps businesses identify potential threats, protect value, improve decision-making, and prepare for uncertainty."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Are internal controls only necessary for large companies?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Growing businesses benefit significantly from establishing appropriate controls before complexity increases."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is the difference between risk management and internal controls?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Risk management focuses on identifying and managing potential risks, while internal controls are the processes and procedures used to reduce those risks."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS help improve existing business processes?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. SHAAS reviews existing processes, identifies weaknesses, and recommends practical improvements to strengthen efficiency and control."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Do investors require strong internal controls?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. Investors and lenders often expect businesses to demonstrate reliable reporting, governance practices, and operational discipline."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Build a More Resilient and Controlled Business",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Strong businesses are not those that eliminate all risks; they are those that understand, manage, and prepare for them."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS helps organisations strengthen risk management, improve internal controls, and build operational resilience while continuing to pursue growth opportunities."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
