    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is the purpose of an internal audit?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Internal audit helps businesses evaluate processes, identify risks, improve controls, and enhance operational effectiveness."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is the difference between internal audit and external audit?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "External audit focuses mainly on providing assurance over financial statements, while internal audit evaluates business processes, controls, risks, and operational effectiveness."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is internal audit only required by large companies?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Growing businesses can benefit significantly from internal audit advisory to establish stronger controls and prepare for future growth."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "How often should a company conduct internal audits?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "The frequency depends on business size, complexity, risk exposure, and industry requirements. Many businesses conduct periodic reviews based on risk priorities."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS perform a one-time internal audit review?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. SHAAS can support businesses with specific internal audit assignments or ongoing advisory support."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Strengthen Your Business Through Better Controls and Insights",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "A strong business requires visibility, accountability, and continuous improvement."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS helps organisations evaluate their processes, identify risks, strengthen controls, and improve operational effectiveness through practical internal audit advisory support."
      },
