    {
     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is organisation design?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Organisation design is the process of creating a structure that aligns people, roles, responsibilities, and processes with business strategy."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "When should a company consider restructuring?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Businesses may consider restructuring when experiencing rapid growth, declining efficiency, strategic changes, mergers, acquisitions, or the need to optimise costs."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is restructuring only about reducing employees?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Restructuring is broader than workforce reduction. It includes improving structures, redefining roles, increasing efficiency, and aligning resources with business objectives."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is organisation structure important?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "A strong organisational structure improves accountability, decision-making, collaboration, and the ability to execute business strategy."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS support companies going through transformation?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Yes. SHAAS supports organisations through transformation by redesigning structures, aligning workforce capabilities, and supporting change implementation."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Build an Organisation Designed for Sustainable Growth",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "The right organisational structure enables businesses to move faster, make better decisions, and execute strategy effectively."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "SHAAS helps organisations design, restructure, and optimise their workforce models to create stronger, more agile, and future-ready organisations."
      },
