    {
     "heading": "What is HR compliance?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "HR compliance refers to ensuring that an organisation’s employment practices, policies, procedures, and workforce processes are aligned with applicable requirements and good business practices."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why is HR compliance important for businesses?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "Effective HR compliance reduces workforce risks, improves consistency, protects business interests, and creates a professional working environment."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is HR compliance only important for large companies?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Startups and SMEs often benefit significantly from establishing proper HR frameworks early to avoid future risks as they grow."
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "What is the difference between HR compliance and employment legal advice?"
      },
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "HR compliance focuses on establishing effective workforce practices and processes, while employment legal advice focuses on specific legal matters and interpretation of employment laws."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS help businesses review existing HR policies?",
