     "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
     "blocks": []
    },
    {
     "heading": "What is HR transformation?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "HR transformation is the process of redesigning HR strategies, processes, technology, and capabilities to better support business objectives."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why should businesses invest in HR technology?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "HR technology improves efficiency, reduces manual work, provides better workforce insights, and enhances employee experience."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Is HR transformation only for large organisations?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "No. Startups and SMEs can benefit from HR transformation by building scalable processes and avoiding inefficient systems as they grow."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "How does HR technology improve business performance?",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "type": "p",
       "text": "HR technology enables better decision-making through improved data, automation, reporting, and more efficient workforce management."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "heading": "Can SHAAS help select an HR system?",
     "blocks": [
